I. Preambul.
The European Union and the Republic of Turkey (hereinafter "the parties"),
In the light of the Protocol to the Association Agreement (hereinafter "the Protocol") between the European Economic Community and Turkey of 23 November 1970 (hereinafter "the Ankara Treaty"), and the decision of the Association Council of 22 May 1971 on its implementation,
With a view to facilitating the accession of Turkey to the European Union and to promoting trade in agricultural products,
Wishing to take into account in the field of agriculture and in particular in the field of fisheries and agriculture products (hereinafter "agricultural products") the interests of the two parties and to promote the harmonious development of economic relations between the parties,
Have adopted the following Protocol:
II.
Chapter 1.
General
Article 1.
1. The Protocol shall apply to agricultural products.
2. For the purposes of this Protocol, 'agricultural products' shall mean products listed in the Annex of this Protocol.
3. The Protocol shall apply only to products covered by the Protocol to the Ankara Treaty and the additional Protocol to the Ankara Treaty.
4. For the purposes of this Protocol, 'common customs tariff' shall mean the common customs tariff of the European Union.
Article 2.
For the purposes of this Protocol:
1. 'Turkey' shall mean the territory of Turkey;
2. 'the European Union' shall mean the territory of the Member States of the European Union;
3. 'the Contracting Parties' shall mean Turkey and the European Union;
4. 'the Association Council' shall mean the Council provided for in Article 22 of the Ankara Treaty;
5. 'importing Party' shall mean the Party importing agricultural products;
6. 'exporting Party' shall mean the Party exporting agricultural products;
7. 'import charge' shall mean any charge, whether ad valorem or otherwise, imposed by the Contracting Parties on products originating in the territory of the other Contracting Party;
8. 'import restrictions' shall mean quotas, import licenses and any other restriction on the import of agricultural products;
